  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Created in an edition of 30.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Created in Fall 2015 by the Studio II class of the Art and the Book Master's Program at the Corcoran School of the Arts and Design at George Washington University, in Washington D.C."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"A collaboration ... under the guidance of instructor Sarah McDermott"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The text was letterpress printed with polymer plates, using Cochin and Adagio Sans typefaces. The maps were screenprinted, and the timelines were digitally printed. The papers used are Somerset Book Heavyweight and Chartham Natural Clear, and the book is bound in a Secret Belgian style"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Features 10 prints by the artists exploring visual responses to sound within the landscape of Washington, D.C. Includes QR codes linked to sound files and sound logs of recordings.</subfield>
  </datafield>
